$ muster mcp --help
Serve muster to agents as an MCP server over stdio (spawned as a child process by a connecting agent). Each call acts on the project containing this folder, or the one --project or $MUSTER_PROJECT names, unless it names another

Usage: muster mcp [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -p, --project <PROJECT>  The project: a registered project's name, or a folder (a value with `/`, or starting with `.` or `~`). Defaults to $MUSTER_PROJECT, then the registered project containing the current folder
      --print-config       Print the JSON config snippet to add muster to an agent's MCP servers, then exit instead of serving
      --as <NAME>          The agent's id on coordination writes and locks; defaults to MUSTER_AGENT, then herdr's pane, then a random session id
  -h, --help               Print help


